answerer sent 1 ARP reply/replies (eth4:1)

awplus# show log
2026 Oct 15 05:44:39 user.notice awplus HSL[936]: ARP_LOG port1.0.48 vlan48 del 00-11-22-33-44-02 (192.168.48.2)
2026 Oct 15 05:44:46 user.notice awplus HSL[936]: ARP_LOG port1.0.48 vlan48 add 00-11-22-33-44-02 (192.168.48.2)
                                         <-- IEEE hyphenated, everything else unchanged

  => STEP 2 PASS: the same MAC, port, VLAN, IP and event pair, rendered
     `00-11-22-33-44-02` (IEEE hyphenated) instead of `0011.2233.4402` (AW+ dotted).
     A direct A/B on events of the same kind, with nothing else in the line changed, so
     the sub-option is proven to do exactly what it claims and no more.

STEP 3 -- removal, both forms, each proven separately                       PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  3a. Remove the sub-option only:
awplus# configure terminal
awplus(config)# no arp log mac-address-format ieee
awplus(config)# end
awplus# show running-config | include arp
arp log                                  <-- the sub-option line is gone, `arp log` remains
awplus# clear log buffered
awplus# clear arp-cache

      leg `L3-fmt-removed`, the same invocation as STEP 2:
awplus# show log
2026 Oct 15 05:45:33 user.notice awplus HSL[936]: ARP_LOG port1.0.48 vlan48 del 0011.2233.4402 (192.168.48.2)
2026 Oct 15 05:45:41 user.notice awplus HSL[936]: ARP_LOG port1.0.48 vlan48 add 0011.2233.4402 (192.168.48.2)

      Logging continues and the MAC has REVERTED to the AW+ dotted form. The removal is
      proven in the log output itself, not only in running-config.

  3b. Remove the feature:
awplus# configure terminal
awplus(config)# no arp log
awplus(config)# end
awplus# show running-config | include arp
awplus#                                  <-- no output: no arp line of any kind
awplus# clear log buffered
awplus# clear arp-cache

      leg `L4-log-removed`, the same invocation again; the responder sent 1 ARP reply,
      so the resolution happened exactly as before.
awplus# show log
ARP_LOG lines: 0

  => STEP 3 PASS: each `no` form is proven separately and behaviourally. Removing the
     sub-option leaves logging working and returns the rendering to the default;
     removing the feature takes the identical leg -- which produced two ARP_LOG lines in
     STEP 1 and two in 3a -- down to none.

